title: Transient relay peek errors surface as monitor lines and wake idle agents
updated_at: "2026-09-25T01:53:50Z"
---
SYMPTOM
c2c monitor peeks the relay inbox every 5s (B089 relay watch). Transient failures each print a line like: relay watch: transient error peeking <node>/<session>: connection_error: Failure("request_timeout") (attempt 1; backing off, will retry). On Grok and Claude every monitor stdout line is a model-visible wake, so idle agents burn turns acknowledging relay noise.

EVIDENCE (2026-09-25, grok session 01a0d5a5-7c00-7d71-a804-91ef2e7f9283 = grok-muse-smart-rjhq, /home/xertrov/src/attn)
- Monitor events at 09:37:06 and 09:46:26 local, each became a task-notification user turn; the agent replied "Another relay timeout. It will retry on its own." (twice).
- Same session started with c2c whoami reporting: registered_unreachable - prior connector sync state exists but the connector is down.
- No double send/recv observed in that session (zero c2c envelopes) - the relay issue there is pure noise/wakes, plus the unreachable-registration state at start.

FIX DIRECTIONS
- Emit relay peek errors only on state change (ok->error once, error->recovered once) or after N consecutive failures, not per transient failure, on surfaces that wake agents.
- Consider suppressing attempt-1 backoff lines entirely.

